  "rationale": "The weight update barely changed the representative error: after a determiner, apples remains far below competing nouns, and several batch errors have the same pattern of a noun completing a determiner/adjective phrase. Add modest support for common batch nouns in that visible syntactic context. Proper names also recur immediately after a comma; support the name class there without predicting one particular name. These are provisional generalizations, not claims that every determiner or comma requires these continuations. They may overboost these words in contexts where other continuations are valid, and the replay gate must check that risk.",
